This step can also be seen another way. Namely, we have to show that there is an étale covering $\{ U_ i \to X\} $ such that $\tilde\xi $ dies in $H^ q(U_ i \times _ X Y, e^{-1}\mathcal{I})$. However, if we prove there is an étale covering $\{ U'_ j \to X'\} $ such that $\tilde\xi $ dies in $H^ q(U'_ i \times _{X'} Y, e^{-1}\mathcal{I})$, then by property (B) for $X' \to X$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/04DQ" data-tag="04DQ">59.43.3</a>) there exists an étale covering $\{ U_ i \to X\} $ such that $U_ i \times _ X X'$ is a disjoint union of schemes over $X'$ each of which factors through $U'_ j$ for some $j$. Thus we see that $\tilde\xi $ dies in $H^ q(U_ i \times _ X Y, e^{-1}\mathcal{I})$ as desired.